## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design CKNE-driven incentives in streaming, including how CKNE affects throughput, partitioning, and latency, plus a stable rebalancing loop and end-to-end validation.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE-to-throughput/partition mapping
- Kafka partition rebalancing and windowing impact
- Baseline SLA guarantees with dynamic prioritization
- Telemetry, monitoring, and stability guarantees

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-mapping for CKNE-driven resource allocation
function mapCKNETokens(ckne, baseThroughput, basePartitions, kappa, lambda, minP, maxP){
  const T = baseThroughput * (1 + kappa * (ckne - 0.5));
  const P = Math.max(minP, Math.min(maxP, Math.round(basePartitions * (1 + lambda * (ckne - 0.5)))));
  return {throughput: T, partitions: P};
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical CKNE-driven canary rollout design for multi-tenant systems, combining edge decision loops with per-tenant state and SLA awareness.

## Key Concepts
- CKNE health integration at edge per tenant
- Canary rollout policy with minute-by-minute loop
- Per-tenant routing and telemetry payloads
- Safety and rollback criteria

## Code Example
```javascript
// minute-by-minute loop (high level)
for (const tenant of tenants) {
  const healthy = health[tenant].latency < 150 && health[tenant].errors < 0.005;
  if (healthy && rollout[tenant] < 40) rollout[tenant] += 5;
  else if (!healthy) rollout[tenant] = 5;
}
```

